{
  "dom_id": "step-q224965",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(4)$ given below, compute $P(3<X\\le 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.2381\\,$ | $\\,0.4335\\,$ | $\\,0.6288\\,$ | $\\,0.7851\\,$ | $\\,0.8893\\,$ | $\\,0.9489\\,$ | $\\,0.9786\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\})+P(X\\in \\{4,5,6,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(3<X\\le 7) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(3<X\\le 7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X\\le 7) & =F(7)-F(3) \\\\  & =0.9489-0.4335 \\\\  & =0.5154.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
